&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is an AI search tool?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An AI search tool or AI search software is any application that uses artificial intelligence to help users crawl, find, retrieve, or synthesize information. But that’s a broad net covering various tools for research, visibility, and optimization.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Here’s how to tell them apart at a glance:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research: Answer engines&lt;/strong&gt; (like ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini) read your question, pull from multiple sources, and return what they think is the best answer. Sources may or may not be cited.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visibility: AI site search tools&lt;/strong&gt; live inside a company’s own website or product. They help visitors find relevant content, answers, or products without leaving the page. Think of the search bar on HubSpot’s website, for example.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimization: AEO (answer engine optimization) tools&lt;/strong&gt; are specifically for marketers. They track whether and how a brand appears in AI search engines and provide data to improve that visibility. Examples include HubSpot AEO and Semrush.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;These three categories—research, visibility, and optimization—often get lumped together, but they shouldn’t be. Knowing which type of tool you’re dealing with helps you determine which tool actually fits your needs. We’ll dig into that more shortly.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How AI Search Tools Are Changing Buyer Research&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Buyers have always done research before making a purchase. What’s changed is where and how far along they get before a vendor ever hears from them.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The numbers speak volumes. &lt;a href="https://www.forrester.com/blogs/b2b_buyers_make_zero_click_buying_number_one/"&gt;Forrester&lt;/a&gt; found that 94% of B2B buyers used AI during recent purchase processes. Of those, 55% used AI to compare vendors, 54% to research products, and 47% to build internal business cases, all before talking to a single sales rep.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI answer engines now rank as the #1 source for vendor research, ahead of vendor websites, sales reps, and product experts.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;On the other end, &lt;a href="https://www.mckinsey.com"&gt;McKinsey research&lt;/a&gt; found that about 50% of consumers across all demographics (including boomers) use AI-powered search for purchasing decisions. In fact, &lt;a href="https://business.adobe.com/blog/the-latest/adobe-digital-insights"&gt;Adobe Digital Insights&lt;/a&gt; reported that 56% of US consumers used generative AI during the 2025 holiday shopping season, up 45% from the year prior.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;So, what does it all mean?&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;By the time a buyer fills out your demo request form or replies to outreach, they’ve likely already consulted an AI engine with many of their questions. According to Forrester, AI answer engines are now the #1 vendor research source, and the buying journey is largely complete before any vendor contact happens.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For marketers, the old playbook of “rank on Google, get traffic” is no longer enough. Visibility inside answer engines is becoming the primary discovery layer, especially for purchase-intent queries.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;The Main Types of AI Search Tools&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Before comparing specific products, it helps to understand the three main categories. Each serves a different person with a different goal.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;1. Answer Engines&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Answer engines are the ChatGPTs and Geminis of the world. Users ask them questions in plain language and get synthesized answers crafted by the tools, drawing from multiple sources.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Some cite their sources; some don’t. Some are real-time and web-connected; some rely on training data. Either way, the goal is to give the user a single response, not just use &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/semantic-search"&gt;semantic search&lt;/a&gt; to deliver resources to filter through, as with a traditional search engine.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Buyers use answer engines for discovery, comparison, and follow-up research. At the same time, &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/ai-marketing"&gt;HubSpot’s AI Trends Report found&lt;/a&gt; 40% of marketers turn to them for research, data analysis, and content generation, &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-b2b-marketing"&gt;among other things&lt;/a&gt;. (This also makes them the most popular AI tool among marketers.)&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketers can’t control what answer engines say about them to consumers, but they can influence it through &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-search-ranking"&gt;answer engine optimization&lt;/a&gt; or sharing credible, well-sourced content that answer engines cite.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;2. AI Site Search Tools&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Ever landed on a clothing website looking for something specific? The search bar at the top of that site is an example of an AI site search tool.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI site search tools are embedded into a company’s website, app, or internal knowledge base. They help users find relevant pages, products, or answers without leaving the page. Platforms like &lt;a href="https://www.algolia.com/"&gt;Algolia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://www.coveo.com/en"&gt;Coveo&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://www.elastic.co/elasticsearch"&gt;Elasticsearch&lt;/a&gt; fall in this bucket.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI site search tools matter most for SaaS companies, e-commerce brands, and enterprises with large content libraries. If visitors can’t find what they’re looking for on your site, they’ll ...

&lt;p&gt;Learning how to optimize your website for AI search is one of the hottest skills for marketers right now, because the audience for these tools is growing fast. Monthly unique visitors to the major answer engines climbed from 634 million in Q1 2025 to 904 million in Q1 2026, up more than 40% in a year, according to &lt;a href="https://www.wix.com/studio/ai-search-lab/research/ai-search-vs-google"&gt;Wix Studio&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=d4233c10-60b6-46d7-9852-c71dde8507b6&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Free AI Search Grader: See Your Brand's Visibility in Answer Engines [Free  Tool]" height="58" width="727" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/d4233c10-60b6-46d7-9852-c71dde8507b6.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But AI search, also known as answer engine optimization (AEO), hasn’t replaced SEO. The two are linked: The fundamentals that earn traditional rankings also open the door to AI citations. Since your customers use both classic search and answer engines to research their options, your business needs to show up in both.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide is built as a repeatable framework that keeps working even as large language models (LLMs) update. I’ll cover the technical setup, the content worth quoting, the differences between engines, and how to tell whether your AI SEO strategy is actually earning traffic.&lt;/p&gt; 
